          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dǎqiú is built from dǎ 'to strike' and qiú 'ball', both inherited from Middle Chinese, taengX and gjuw (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), though dǎ is not the sound taengX would regularly give. The dictionary glosses gjuw as 'fine jade', and under another way of writing it as a ball of fur that is struck."
            }
